WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.240
Ready to suit up, Keanu?

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:06.840
During this year's San Diego Comic-Con, filmmaker
and comic book geek Kevin Smith had a chance

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.011
to chat with Avengers: Endgame directors Joe
and Anthony Russo and the three of them had

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.709
a little chat about Keanu Reeves' place in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:14.709 --> 00:00:18.720
Speculation over Reeves joining the MCU has
recently grown to a fever pitch.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.529
The actor's career has been enjoying a stellar
resurgence thanks in large part to the highly

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:27.019
successful John Wick franchise, and he and
the MCU seem like a match made in Hollywood

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:27.540
heaven.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.080
"Yeah, I'm thinking I'm back."

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.600
Marvel Studios head honcho Kevin Feige recently
threw fuel on the rumor fire by suggesting

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.550
that Reeves has been considered for virtually
every movie Marvel has ever made, and that

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.829
the only reason he hasn't shown up so far
is that they simply haven't found the right

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:43.829
part for him.

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:47.570
If it were up to Smith and the Russo brothers,
however, Reeves would be donning a white bodysuit,

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:52.780
cape, and cowl and stepping into the role
of Marc Spector, otherwise known as Moon Knight.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.600
During their comic-con interview, Smith posed
a simple question to the Russo brothers: who

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.960
would they like to see Reeves play in the
MCU?

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.879
Much hemming and hawing ensued, with the Russos
admitting that the choices were pretty much

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:07.390
limitless, before Smith offered up Moon Knight
as his pick prompting Joe Russo to reply:

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.610
"Right, that's a good call."

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:12.660
Just like Keanu, it seems to be more a matter
of when, not if, Moon Knight will eventually

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.640
appear in the MCU.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.000
Considered by some to be Marvel's answer to
Batman, Marc Spector is a one-time mercenary

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.680
who suffers from dissociative identity disorder.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.210
On assignment in Egypt, he had a transformative
experience when his life was spared by the

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.840
ancient god Khonshu.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.940
In return, he agreed to serve Khonshu on Earth.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.970
With the help of his right-hand man Frenchie
and his significant other Marlene, Spector

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:37.850
uses his considerable fortune to equip himself
as the costumed vigilante Moon Knight, becoming

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.920
the bane of the New York City criminal underworld.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:44.850
"I, the moon's knight of vengeance, must carry
out your luminous will.”

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.020
“Ah… are you seriously talking to the
moon?

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.920
As in, the cow jumped over?"

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.560
The character has long been a favorite of
Marvel comics fans, and it was suggested early

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:57.560
and often that he would lend himself well
to a Netflix series a notion that sadly became

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.880
moot when Marvel Television ended its relationship
with the streaming service in 2019.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.860
As recently as last year, however, Feige remarked
that Moon Knight was one of the characters

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.061
being eyed for a potential MCU solo feature
but there was no mention of the character

00:02:10.061 --> 00:02:14.410
during the recent reveal of Marvel's Phase
4 slate at Comic-Con, meaning that any such

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:17.880
project isn't likely to come to fruition for
at least a few years.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:21.780
Ultimately, this makes it almost certain that,
when Marc Spector finally shows up in the

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.070
MCU, he won't be portrayed by Reeves.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:27.730
Sure, the star has proven his action skills
with the John Wick series, but when it comes

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.890
to casting, Marvel is in the midst of something
of a youth movement.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:35.170
The studio famously likes to sign its featured
players to multiple-picture deals stretching

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.800
over several years which is part of the reason
why, for example, Feige has stated his intention

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.070
to go younger for the actors he will eventually
cast as the X-Men.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.930
And since Endgame will likely be the final
Marvel movie to be directed by Joe and Anthony

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.500
Russo, the ace filmmakers basically have no
horse in the race.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.850
As cool as it would be to see Reeves don Moon
Knight's cowl, it seems unlikely that the

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:58.320
54-year old actor would be able to remain
in the role for the five to 10 years that

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.430
Marvel would demand of him.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:02.680
Of course, it goes without saying that Feige
and his team are very, very good at their

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.220
jobs.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.080
And when Marvel finally announces Reeves's
role in the MCU, you can bet your bottom dollar

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.320
that it'll prove to be the perfect match.

